   "text": {
    "L1": "Metals and non-metals have different common properties.",
    "L2": "Metals are usually shiny, hard, malleable, ductile, sonorous and good conductors.",
    "L3": "Malleability makes aluminium into thin foil, and ductility draws copper into thin wires.",
    "L4": "Sonority makes a temple bell ring, while conduction helps metals carry heat to food.",
    "L5": "Non-metals are usually dull, brittle, not sonorous and poor conductors.",
    "L6": "To identify an unknown rod, use more than one test: look, tap, bend and test conduction.",
    "L7": "Shine alone is not enough, because iodine is a shiny non-metal.",
    "L8": "Here is a magnet check: it attracts iron, nickel, cobalt and things made with them, not every metal.",
    "L9": "Choose the material that the magnet will pull."
   },
